    ('48e08ccf-7661-47c1-9a0e-ff9e205530e0'::uuid, 'card_description', NULL, '3rd-millennium BC Dilmun burial mound field in the Northern Governorate. Inscribed as UNESCO World Heritage in 2019 as part of the Dilmun Burial Mounds, it marks a civilisation''s funerary landscape.', 'teaser-card-s033-rollback:48e08ccf-7661-47c1-9a0e-ff9e205530e0:card_description', 'rollback of teaser-card-s033: card_description "3rd-millennium BC Dilmun burial mound field in the Northern Governorate. Inscribed as UNESCO World Heritage in 2019 as part of the Dilmun Burial Mounds, it marks a civilisation''s funerary landscape." restored on Jannusan Burial Mound Field', '||e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855', '[{"source": "lane WB run wb-cardgap-2026-10-07: no-description", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-cardgap-2026-10-07/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "no-description"}]'::jsonb),
    ('49cd7035-b70c-4991-b776-e5ae204ad8c5'::uuid, 'card_description', 'In the Orne department of Normandy, Habloville holds two Neolithic monuments: a stone table measuring 3.25 by 2.95 metres, and just to the south a listed tumulus.', NULL, 'teaser-card-s033-rollback:49cd7035-b70c-4991-b776-e5ae204ad8c5:card_description', 'rollback of teaser-card-s033: card_description None restored on Habloville', '7cb12871467758e86b882033be4f6e65055d7ad806eea73e25364282a6bd833c|847505ab9ad0761b836f0ab0f84acc0bce07bac62b4c9c6771551f7f6d51db85|847505ab9ad0761b836f0ab0f84acc0bce07bac62b4c9c6771551f7f6d51db85', '[{"source": "lane WB run wb-cardgap-2026-10-07: writer teaser-write-006", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-cardgap-2026-10-07/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "In the Orne department of Normandy, Habloville holds two Neolithic monuments: a stone table measuring 3.25 by 2.95 metres, and just to the south a listed tumulus."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-cardgap-2026-10-07: checker teaser-check-006 (check), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-cardgap-2026-10-07/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Habloville is in the Orne department of Normandy [S1]; Habloville holds two Neolithic monuments [S1]; one is a stone table (dolmen) measuring 3.25 by 2.95 metres [S2]; just to the south lies a listed tumulus [S3]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-cardgap-2026-10-07: verifier teaser-verify-018 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-cardgap-2026-10-07/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Habloville holds two Neolithic monuments, a dolmen and a tumulus site. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Habloville]; Habloville is in the Orne department of Normandy. [SUPPORTED: https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Habloville]; The stone table (dolmen) measures 3.25 by 2.95 metres. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Habloville]; The tumulus lies just to the south of the dolmen. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Habloville]; The tumulus is a listed (monument historique) monument, classed in 1968. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Habloville]"}]'::jsonb),
    ('4a07cc38-1b55-4254-b0ad-fe875310caf7'::uuid, 'card_description', 'The Temple of Augustus, probably built between 27 BC and AD 14, measures about 8 by 17.3 m and 14 m high, its tetrastyle prostyle porch of Corinthian columns standing on a podium.', NULL, 'teaser-card-s033-rollback:4a07cc38-1b55-4254-b0ad-fe875310caf7:card_description', 'rollback of teaser-card-s033: card_description None restored on Temple of Augustus, Pula', '96a15568c9f808e14472987def39890d5d58f7f38a69e66df69698901cef6c09|82a4bedb7bac8bc0fa07f4287fefaea2839b0754c045e038ae5b32e4e384b462|82a4bedb7bac8bc0fa07f4287fefaea2839b0754c045e038ae5b32e4e384b462', '[{"source": "lane WB run wb-cardgap-2026-10-07: writer teaser-rewrite1-001", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-cardgap-2026-10-07/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "The Temple of Augustus, probably built between 27 BC and AD 14, measures about 8 by 17.3 m and 14 m high, its tetrastyle prostyle porch of Corinthian columns standing on a podium."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-cardgap-2026-10-07: checker teaser-check1-001 (check1), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-cardgap-2026-10-07/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "the temple was probably built between 27 BC and AD 14 [S2]; it measures about 8 by 17.3 m [S3]; it is 14 m high [S3]; it has a tetrastyle prostyle porch of Corinthian columns [S3]; the porch stands on a podium [S3]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-cardgap-2026-10-07: verifier teaser-verify-018 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-cardgap-2026-10-07/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "The site is a Roman temple dedicated to Augustus at Pula, Croatia. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Temple_of_Augustus,_Pula]; It was probably built between 27 BC and AD 14. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Temple_of_Augustus,_Pula]; It measures about 8 by 17.3 m. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Temple_of_Augustus,_Pula]; It is 14 m high. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Temple_of_Augustus,_Pula]; It has a tetrastyle prostyle porch of Corinthian columns. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Temple_of_Augustus,_Pula]; The porch stands on a podium. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Temple_of_Augustus,_Pula]"}]'::jsonb),
    ('4a1c0e1a-7ef6-4e1f-bbdb-6334304bcf52'::uuid, 'card_description', 'At Ras Shamra the port city of Ugarit held a royal palace of many courtyards and two acropolis temples to Baal and Dagan; its excavated texts echo Hebrew biblical poetry.', NULL, 'teaser-card-s033-rollback:4a1c0e1a-7ef6-4e1f-bbdb-6334304bcf52:card_description', 'rollback of teaser-card-s033: card_description None restored on Ugarit', '0b32e5dc95b8c26913f521821c82fb954e255b6ecd693ee7371cc3704ad67690|d2d30301c815ce3f09fb42abd65992fafa5ff1e7b2a2d7e3daa5bdd5608a7bd8|d2d30301c815ce3f09fb42abd65992fafa5ff1e7b2a2d7e3daa5bdd5608a7bd8', '[{"source": "lane WB run wb-cardgap-2026-10-07: writer teaser-write-006", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-cardgap-2026-10-07/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "At Ras Shamra the port city of Ugarit held a royal palace of many courtyards and two acropolis temples to Baal and Dagan; its excavated texts echo Hebrew biblical poetry."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-cardgap-2026-10-07: checker teaser-check-006 (check), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-cardgap-2026-10-07/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Ugarit was a port city at Ras Shamra [S1]; it had a royal palace with multiple courtyards [S2]; it had two acropolis temples dedicated to Baal and Dagan [S2]; its excavated texts have parallels to Hebrew biblical poetry [S3]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-cardgap-2026-10-07: verifier teaser-verify-018 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-cardgap-2026-10-07/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Ugarit was a port city. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ugarit]; The city lay at Ras Shamra in northern Syria. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ugarit]; Ugarit had a royal palace whose rooms were arranged around courtyards. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ugarit]; Its acropolis carried two temples, to Baal and to Dagan. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ugarit]; The two temples are the Temple of Baal and the Temple of Dagan. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ugarit]; The texts excavated at Ugarit echo Hebrew biblical poetry (psalms show influence from Ugaritic texts). [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Psalms]"}]'::jsonb),
    ('4b635088-8799-4dc1-99de-b2b224a71d28'::uuid, 'card_description', 'The Town Walks of Dorchester follow the line of the Roman defences of Durnovaria, its ruined walls landscaped into tree-lined avenues between 1702 and 1743. Only one wall fragment survives.', NULL, 'teaser-card-s033-rollback:4b635088-8799-4dc1-99de-b2b224a71d28:card_description', 'rollback of teaser-card-s033: card_description None restored on Town Walks, Dorchester', '6207e68c096b20a4a11693f01cbcd53574481f95df6d7e405cbbe2ff2802dca2|7db0b4301f4afec4aca2ecd646f1168309b93cb79dcdbc7eee27c28fb180e0b7|7db0b4301f4afec4aca2ecd646f1168309b93cb79dcdbc7eee27c28fb180e0b7', '[{"source": "lane WB run wb-cardgap-2026-10-07: writer teaser-write-007", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-cardgap-2026-10-07/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "The Town Walks of Dorchester follow the line of the Roman defences of Durnovaria, its ruined walls landscaped into tree-lined avenues between 1702 and 1743. Only one wall fragment survives."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-cardgap-2026-10-07: checker teaser-check-007 (check), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-cardgap-2026-10-07/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "the Town Walks of Dorchester follow the line of the Roman defences of Durnovaria [S1]; the ruined walls were landscaped into tree-lined avenues between 1702 and 1743 [S4]; only one wall fragment survives [S5]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-cardgap-2026-10-07: verifier teaser-verify-019 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-cardgap-2026-10-07/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "The Town Walks are a series of public walks in Dorchester running along the former Roman defences of the town [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Town_Walks,_Dorchester]; The Roman town whose defences the walks follow was called Durnovaria [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Town_Walks,_Dorchester]; The Roman walls were already ruined/mostly destroyed before the walks were laid out [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Town_Walks,_Dorchester]; Between 1702 and 1743 the Roman embankments were landscaped to form a series of walks [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Town_Walks,_Dorchester]; The walks are tree-lined avenues laid out on the line of the Roman defences [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Town_Walks,_Dorchester]; Only one fragment of the Roman town walls survives [SUPPORTED: https://britishlistedbuildings.co.uk/101220733-roman-wall-dorchester]"}]'::jsonb),
    ('4c4c07a0-d94d-42fa-b1f2-a4f4ab3b8094'::uuid, 'card_description', 'Ražanj stands on the ancient Via Militaris, the Roman military highway. The settlement on it was known as Cametas in Roman times, and finds from building work confirm prehistoric habitation.', NULL, 'teaser-card-s033-rollback:4c4c07a0-d94d-42fa-b1f2-a4f4ab3b8094:card_description', 'rollback of teaser-card-s033: card_description None restored on Ražanj', '089dc20859e4f8adf93521f90b59b282273579d8783ef7a41fd54b63c53a7604|3a7fb83e63019554dfac5894ad83d440f01cb2c33281a3fcc398247219fbbd32|3a7fb83e63019554dfac5894ad83d440f01cb2c33281a3fcc398247219fbbd32', '[{"source": "lane WB run wb-cardgap-2026-10-07: writer teaser-rewrite1-001", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-cardgap-2026-10-07/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Ražanj stands on the ancient Via Militaris, the Roman military highway. The settlement on it was known as Cametas in Roman times, and finds from building work confirm prehistoric habitation."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-cardgap-2026-10-07: checker teaser-check1-001 (check1), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-cardgap-2026-10-07/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Razanj stands on the ancient Via Militaris [S1]; Via Militaris was the Roman military highway [S1]; the settlement was known as Cametas in Roman times [S2]; finds recovered during construction work confirm habitation from prehistoric times [S3]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-cardgap-2026-10-07: verifier teaser-verify-019 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-cardgap-2026-10-07/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Ražanj is a village/settlement in Serbia [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ra%C5%BEanj]; Ražanj lies on the ancient highway [SUPPORTED: https://www.turizamrazanj.rs/en/cultural-heritage/]; The road at Ražanj was the Via Militaris [SUPPORTED: https://www.turizamrazanj.rs/en/cultural-heritage/]; The Via Militaris is an ancient Roman road [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Via_Militaris]; The Via Militaris is a Roman military road (military highway) [SUPPORTED: https://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Via_Militaris_(Balkan)]; The settlement was known as Cametas in Roman times [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ra%C5%BEanj]; Building work produced archaeological finds that confirm the settlement existed in prehistoric times [SUPPORTED: https://razanj.ls.gov.rs/en/discover-razanj/history/]; The area was inhabited in prehistoric times [SUPPORTED: https://razanj.ls.gov.rs/en/discover-razanj/history/]"}]'::jsonb),
    ('4c6f2c0a-abdb-4a1d-a12c-a71403776fe4'::uuid, 'card_description', 'Koufonisi is an uninhabited islet in the Libyan Sea, 5.6 km south of cape Goudero on Crete''s eastern coast. Through the summer, tour boats cross from the port of Makry Gialos.', NULL, 'teaser-card-s033-rollback:4c6f2c0a-abdb-4a1d-a12c-a71403776fe4:card_description', 'rollback of teaser-card-s033: card_description None restored on Koufonisi, Crete', '98ab826978eeb7ed9de7986cf42a519ff385ba5b792939eff07b5e4a4e2e73f9|7f0ba9905e50b0c4b7020e5232c4e6541f860f8e1f81a1338c195af23b40a19e|7f0ba9905e50b0c4b7020e5232c4e6541f860f8e1f81a1338c195af23b40a19e', '[{"source": "lane WB run wb-cardgap-2026-10-07: writer teaser-write-007", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-cardgap-2026-10-07/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Koufonisi is an uninhabited islet in the Libyan Sea, 5.6 km south of cape Goudero on Crete''s eastern coast. Through the summer, tour boats cross from the port of Makry Gialos."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-cardgap-2026-10-07: checker teaser-check-007 (check), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-cardgap-2026-10-07/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Koufonisi is an uninhabited islet in the Libyan Sea [S1]; it lies 5.6 km south of cape Goudero on Crete''s eastern coast [S1]; tour boats come from the port of Makry Gialos during the summer [S2]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-cardgap-2026-10-07: verifier teaser-verify-019 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-cardgap-2026-10-07/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Koufonisi is an uninhabited Greek islet lying off eastern Crete in the Libyan Sea [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Koufonisi_(Crete)]; Koufonisi is an islet (a small island), not a mainland site [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Koufonisi_(Crete)]; Koufonisi is uninhabited [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Koufonisi_(Crete)]; Koufonisi lies in the Libyan Sea [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Koufonisi_(Crete)]; Koufonisi lies 5.6 km south of cape Goudero [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Koufonisi_(Crete)]; Koufonisi lies off the eastern coast of Crete [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Koufonisi_(Crete)]; Through the summer, tour boats cross to the island from the port of Makry Gialos [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Koufonisi_(Crete)]"}]'::jsonb),
    ('4cab063f-a1a1-4e24-a46a-d609f2f87f53'::uuid, 'card_description', NULL, 'Rock painting site in the Huamalíes highlands, dated broadly to the 1st millennium BC. One of many rock art sites scattered across the upper Huánuco Region at high altitude.', 'teaser-card-s033-rollback:4cab063f-a1a1-4e24-a46a-d609f2f87f53:card_description', 'rollback of teaser-card-s033: card_description ''Rock painting site in the Huamalíes highlands, dated broadly to the 1st millennium BC. One of many rock art sites scattered across the upper Huánuco Region at high altitude.'' restored on Quillcay Machay', '||e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855', '[{"source": "lane WB run wb-cardgap-2026-10-07: no-description", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-cardgap-2026-10-07/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "no-description"}]'::jsonb),
    ('4cdbbcf7-6cdf-4295-be70-8f77b1e92bf4'::uuid, 'card_description', 'Hardknott Roman Fort, the remains of Mediobogdum, stands on the western side of the challenging Hardknott Pass. Leather objects from its Roman occupation have been found here.', NULL, 'teaser-card-s033-rollback:4cdbbcf7-6cdf-4295-be70-8f77b1e92bf4:card_description', 'rollback of teaser-card-s033: card_description None restored on Hardknott Roman Fort', 'b080de4f2817286ea21aa466b743b291f84c9f207e034552ab082b0a3cf89933|a722ef88bb4eba61772685439fd87813bc1290217144d6748d0b94be7652f440|a722ef88bb4eba61772685439fd87813bc1290217144d6748d0b94be7652f440', '[{"source": "lane WB run wb-cardgap-2026-10-07: writer teaser-write-007", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-cardgap-2026-10-07/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Hardknott Roman Fort, the remains of Mediobogdum, stands on the western side of the challenging Hardknott Pass. Leather objects from its Roman occupation have been found here."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-cardgap-2026-10-07: checker teaser-check-007 (check), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-cardgap-2026-10-07/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Hardknott Roman Fort is the remains of the Roman fort Mediobogdum [S1]; it stands on the western side of the challenging Hardknott Pass [S1]; leather objects from its Roman occupation have been found at the site [S4]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-cardgap-2026-10-07: verifier teaser-verify-019 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-cardgap-2026-10-07/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Hardknott is an archaeological site consisting of the remains of a Roman fort [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hardknott_Fort]; The Roman fort was named Mediobogdum [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hardknott_Fort]; The fort stands on the western side of Hardknott Pass [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hardknott_Fort]; Hardknott Pass is a challenging pass [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hardknott_Fort]; Leather objects from the Roman occupation have been found at the site [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hardknott_Fort]"}]'::jsonb),
    ('4f366f34-983c-42e1-a89d-7e8f5f77cdce'::uuid, 'card_description', 'At 2,430 meters, about 104 caves and rock shelters around Machu Picchu held the remains of about 174 individuals, interpreted largely as yanaconas rather than the Inca elite.', NULL, 'teaser-card-s033-rollback:4f366f34-983c-42e1-a89d-7e8f5f77cdce:card_description', 'rollback of teaser-card-s033: card_description None restored on Machu Picchu', 'e07dec0c4885e3a99b4e7f75753c39cc431f80b3f11c9db59c574b58430bd79f|c2398fffdc17f4935396e3f988a8ff2a1080c6cf69340a8dd57859365762daa3|c2398fffdc17f4935396e3f988a8ff2a1080c6cf69340a8dd57859365762daa3', '[{"source": "lane WB run wb-cardgap-2026-10-07: writer teaser-write-007", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-cardgap-2026-10-07/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "At 2,430 meters, about 104 caves and rock shelters around Machu Picchu held the remains of about 174 individuals, interpreted largely as yanaconas rather than the Inca elite."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-cardgap-2026-10-07: checker teaser-check-007 (check), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-cardgap-2026-10-07/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "the site is at 2,430 meters [S1]; about 104 caves and rock shelters around Machu Picchu served as burial chambers [S3]; they contained the remains of about 174 individuals [S3]; those remains are interpreted as largely belonging to yanaconas rather than the Inca elite [S3]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-cardgap-2026-10-07: verifier teaser-verify-019 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-cardgap-2026-10-07/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "The subject is a set of burial caves and rock shelters around the Machu Picchu site that held human remains [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Machu_Picchu]; About 104 caves and rock shelters were documented around Machu Picchu [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Machu_Picchu]; Those caves and rock shelters held the remains of about 174 individuals [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Machu_Picchu]; The remains are interpreted largely as yanaconas rather than the Inca elite [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Machu_Picchu]; Machu Picchu stands at 2,430 metres above sea level [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Machu_Picchu]"}]'::jsonb),
    ('4f89dada-27a0-4c49-bc79-5fc5ef812766'::uuid, 'card_description', 'Craterus'' ex voto at Delphi was a bronze lion hunt with Alexander the Great. French excavations uncovered walls standing 4m high between the Temple of Apollo and the theatre.', NULL, 'teaser-card-s033-rollback:4f89dada-27a0-4c49-bc79-5fc5ef812766:card_description', 'rollback of teaser-card-s033: card_description None restored on Craterus'' ex voto', '42985bb5e990e1be10335f5f542aee7383927b2e572d43b7f06e558e02b0dd89|b0f976d7523951eb50b09022e0e03892c3fb2c8e9f7bff056f7e5cac984a9110|b0f976d7523951eb50b09022e0e03892c3fb2c8e9f7bff056f7e5cac984a9110', '[{"source": "lane WB run wb-cardgap-2026-10-07: writer teaser-write-007", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-cardgap-2026-10-07/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Craterus'' ex voto at Delphi was a bronze lion hunt with Alexander the Great. French excavations uncovered walls standing 4m high between the Temple of Apollo and the theatre."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-cardgap-2026-10-07: checker teaser-check-007 (check), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-cardgap-2026-10-07/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Craterus'' ex voto at Delphi was a bronze sculptural group depicting a lion hunt [S1]; the hunt involved Alexander the Great [S1]; French excavations uncovered walls standing 4m high [S2]; the building lies between the Temple of Apollo and the theatre [S2]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-cardgap-2026-10-07: verifier teaser-verify-020 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-cardgap-2026-10-07/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Craterus'' ex voto is a votive monument at Delphi, the ex voto of the Macedonian general Craterus [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Craterus%27_ex_voto]; The monument was a bronze sculpted complex dedicated at Delphi (Plutarch''s account) [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Craterus%27_ex_voto]; The sculpture depicted a lion hunt, an incident of Alexander''s life in which Craterus saved him [SUPPORT