    ('6b0c9ab6-58dd-4989-a937-b83a957ef665'::uuid, 'card_description', NULL, '3rd century AD. One of three burial mounds at Bergama — 140 m wide, 26 m tall, 80,000 cubic metres of earth. Believed to be Europe''s tallest open pyramid-style tomb, still only partially excavated.', 'teaser-card-s033-rollback:6b0c9ab6-58dd-4989-a937-b83a957ef665:card_description', 'rollback of teaser-card-s033: card_description "3rd century AD. One of three burial mounds at Bergama — 140 m wide, 26 m tall, 80,000 cubic metres of earth. Believed to be Europe''s tallest open pyramid-style tomb, still only partially excavated." restored on Maltepe Tumulus', '||e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855', '[{"source": "lane WB run wb-cardgap-2026-10-07: no-description", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-cardgap-2026-10-07/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "no-description"}]'::jsonb),
    ('6c736688-98d7-4c57-bf53-1f4367950131'::uuid, 'card_description', 'At Le Grand-Pressigny, carvers struck blades up to 40 cm long from caramel-coloured flint and sent them to the Alps, Brittany and Holland. The mines were active around 3000 BC.', NULL, 'teaser-card-s033-rollback:6c736688-98d7-4c57-bf53-1f4367950131:card_description', 'rollback of teaser-card-s033: card_description None restored on Le Grand-Pressigny', '15e50878029f849046c3de6c658753e487743a91ba9a88b6f4585eca01e87e8b|5822e7ab3359f9cea42ea7706b961e92ab57b31da0dcebe36b49a354f94291f5|5822e7ab3359f9cea42ea7706b961e92ab57b31da0dcebe36b49a354f94291f5', '[{"source": "lane WB run wb-cardgap-2026-10-07: writer teaser-write-009", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-cardgap-2026-10-07/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "At Le Grand-Pressigny, carvers struck blades up to 40 cm long from caramel-coloured flint and sent them to the Alps, Brittany and Holland. The mines were active around 3000 BC."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-cardgap-2026-10-07: checker teaser-check-009 (check), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-cardgap-2026-10-07/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "at Le Grand-Pressigny carvers struck blades up to 40 cm long [S2]; the blades were struck from caramel-coloured flint [S2]; the blades were sent to the Alps, Brittany and Holland [S2]; the site was active around 3000 BC [S1]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-cardgap-2026-10-07: verifier teaser-verify-027 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-cardgap-2026-10-07/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Le Grand-Pressigny is a prehistoric flint mine (a Chalcolithic flint mine) in France [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Le_Grand-Pressigny]; Carvers at Le Grand-Pressigny struck large flint blades by indirect percussion [SUPPORTED: https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grand-Pressigny]; The blades reach nearly 40 cm in length [SUPPORTED: https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grand-Pressigny]; The flint is caramel-coloured [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Le_Grand-Pressigny]; The Pressignien blades/daggers were exported as far as Switzerland, an Alpine country (the card calls this destination the Alps) [SUPPORTED: https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grand-Pressigny]; Grand-Pressigny flint was imported into Brittany [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prehistory_of_Brittany]; The stone was exported as far as the Netherlands (Holland) [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Le_Grand-Pressigny]; The Grand-Pressigny flint was intensively exploited in the early 3rd millennium BC (around 2800 BC, i.e. around 3000 BC) [SUPPORTED: https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/IIIe_mill%C3%A9naire_av._J.-C.]"}]'::jsonb),
    ('6cf9cf72-ba27-4843-bbd4-e9acfabec124'::uuid, 'card_description', 'Wanakawri is a legendary mountain and an archaeological site at 4,089 metres, one of the highest elevations near Cusco. It was one of the most important wak''as of the Inca culture.', NULL, 'teaser-card-s033-rollback:6cf9cf72-ba27-4843-bbd4-e9acfabec124:card_description', 'rollback of teaser-card-s033: card_description None restored on Wanakawri, Cusco', '674f05bcdd24139d3b4ac72d4f8fd5cc803e0109f4e3c457019aaca9721ed73d|acbe919e8cb034bda965a112798cfe32c2ddd57ece20c41e3b0d9dfb7132309c|acbe919e8cb034bda965a112798cfe32c2ddd57ece20c41e3b0d9dfb7132309c', '[{"source": "lane WB run wb-cardgap-2026-10-07: writer teaser-write-009", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-cardgap-2026-10-07/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Wanakawri is a legendary mountain and an archaeological site at 4,089 metres, one of the highest elevations near Cusco. It was one of the most important wak''as of the Inca culture."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-cardgap-2026-10-07: checker teaser-check-009 (check), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-cardgap-2026-10-07/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Wanakawri is a legendary mountain [S1]; Wanakawri is an archaeological site [S1]; the mountain with the archaeological remains is 4,089 metres high [S3]; it is one of the highest elevations near Cusco [S3]; Wanakawri was one of the most important wak''as of the Inca culture [S4]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-cardgap-2026-10-07: verifier teaser-verify-027 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-cardgap-2026-10-07/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Wanakawri (the Cusco site) is an archaeological site [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wanakawri]; Wanakawri is a legendary mountain in Peru [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wanakawri]; The mountain with the archaeological remains is 4,089 metres high [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wanakawri]; It is one of the highest elevations near Cusco [SUPPORTED: h