    ('96395824-9c31-477a-bf51-13ecb5035d56'::uuid, 'card_description', 'Pintia was besieged and destroyed by the Romans, and with it went the Vaccean culture, religion and language. The zone has three parts: a city, a necropolis and a potter''s district.', NULL, 'teaser-card-s033-rollback:96395824-9c31-477a-bf51-13ecb5035d56:card_description', 'rollback of teaser-card-s033: card_description None restored on Pintia', 'aa362a9e7ccbe3f65d8e335d4f10ff6979ce5c62778b722482d87760b8fa5e5f|bd17b9cd25bc0d72f56eabe8d02a8c8e5671bc0a1a36f8f5638bfa183e53fc69|bd17b9cd25bc0d72f56eabe8d02a8c8e5671bc0a1a36f8f5638bfa183e53fc69', '[{"source": "lane WB run wb-cardgap-2026-10-07: writer teaser-write-011", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-cardgap-2026-10-07/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Pintia was besieged and destroyed by the Romans, and with it went the Vaccean culture, religion and language. The zone has three parts: a city, a necropolis and a potter''s district."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-cardgap-2026-10-07: checker teaser-check-011 (check), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-cardgap-2026-10-07/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Pintia was besieged and destroyed by the Romans [S1]; with Pintia went the Vaccean culture, religion and language [S1]; the zone consists of three parts [S3]; the three parts are a city, a necropolis and a potter''s district [S3]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-cardgap-2026-10-07: verifier teaser-verify-031 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-cardgap-2026-10-07/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Pintia is an ancient city of the Vaccaei [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pintia]; Pintia was besieged and destroyed by the Romans [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pintia]; With Pintia went the Vaccean culture [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pintia]; With Pintia went the Vaccean religion [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pintia]; With Pintia went the Vaccean language [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pintia]; The archaeological zone consists of three different parts [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pintia]; One of the parts is the city of Las Quintanas [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pintia]; One of the parts is the necropolis of Las Ruedas [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pintia]; One of the parts is a potter''s district [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pintia]"}]'::jsonb),
    ('97fb3d8b-5f53-4233-a31e-80c6b2b5228a'::uuid, 'card_description', 'Daskalio, a tiny islet off Keros in the Cyclades, was once a promontory before the sea rose. Metalworking workshops dating from 2500 BCE were found there, and Naxos marble terraces it.', NULL, 'teaser-card-s033-rollback:97fb3d8b-5f53-4233-a31e-80c6b2b5228a:card_description', 'rollback of teaser-card-s033: card_description None restored on Daskalio', '0b1063d7a8deb170653cc546d97025f0e344557c6b6708119ee86183ca88cb9e|50b837ef9f187082b9349f8f7448891fee2bee36f5f0a0fdf9ee277199a1d847|50b837ef9f187082b9349f8f7448891fee2bee36f5f0a0fdf9ee277199a1d847', '[{"source": "lane WB run wb-cardgap-2026-10-07: writer teaser-rewrite-v-002", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-cardgap-2026-10-07/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Daskalio, a tiny islet off Keros in the Cyclades, was once a promontory before the sea rose. Metalworking workshops dating from 2500 BCE were found there, and Naxos marble terraces it."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-cardgap-2026-10-07: checker teaser-check-v-002 (check-v), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-cardgap-2026-10-07/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "the card names the site Daskalio [S1]; it is a tiny islet off Keros in the Cyclades [S1]; it was once a promontory before the sea rose [S2]; metalworking workshops dating from 2500 BCE were found there [S3]; it is terraced with Naxos marble [S4]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-cardgap-2026-10-07: verifier teaser-verify2-004 (verify2), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-cardgap-2026-10-07/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Daskalio is a tiny islet off Keros, in the Cyclades of Greece [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Daskalio]; Daskalio lies just off the west coast of the larger island of Keros [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Daskalio]; Daskalio was formerly a promontory of Keros and is now an islet because of sea level rise [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Daskalio]; Evidence of advanced metalworking workshops was found at Daskalio [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Daskalio]; The metalworking workshops found at Daskalio date from 2500 BCE [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Daskalio]; Daskalio was extensively terraced [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Daskalio]; The terracing of Daskalio used marble quarried on the island of Naxos [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Daskalio]; More than 1,000 tons of marble were used in the terracing of Daskalio [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Daskalio]"}]'::jsonb),
    ('996e0b32-f8ca-4d04-8900-ed937b729269'::uuid, 'card_description', 'Five caves on the western shore of the Mani Peninsula make up Apidima Cave. Apidima 2, with Neanderthal morphology, was dated to more than 170,000 years; Apidima 1 is older.', NULL, 'teaser-card-s033-rollback:996e0b32-f8ca-4d04-8900-ed937b729269:card_description', 'rollback of teaser-card-s033: card_description None restored on Apidima Cave', '80944cd438ece8ce5de4593ef57f0017f9d2447e1abb85791ad38056f0ead50a|e3837d14ce6b6e6fc328f959f5e804b9d8322e2eb050221081eb231305c71d0a|e3837d14ce6b6e6fc328f959f5e804b9d8322e2eb050221081eb231305c71d0a', '[{"source": "lane WB run wb-cardgap-2026-10-07: writer teaser-write-011", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-cardgap-2026-10-07/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Five caves on the western shore of the Mani Peninsula make up Apidima Cave. Apidima 2, with Neanderthal morphology, was dated to more than 170,000 years; Apidima 1 is older."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-cardgap-2026-10-07: checker teaser-check-011 (check), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-cardgap-2026-10-07/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Apidima Cave is a complex of five caves [S1]; it is on the western shore of the Mani Peninsula [S1]; Apidima 2 has Neanderthal morphology [S5]; Apidima 2 was dated to more than 170,000 years [S5]; Apidima 1 is older [S6]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-cardgap-2026-10-07: verifier teaser-verify-032 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-cardgap-2026-10-07/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Apidima Cave is a complex of five caves [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apidima_Cave]; The cave complex lies on the western shore of the Mani Peninsula in southern Greece [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apidima_Cave]; Apidima 2 has Neanderthal morphology [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apidima_Cave]; Apidima 2 was dated to more than 170,000 years old [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apidima_Cave]; Apidima 1 is the older